      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CANTILEVER (3) gets the nod after a sound second-up platform, having led and held third at this venue when beaten just over a length in a small field. He is proven at this track and distance, has strong recent-season figures and gets a winning rider back. Fitter for that run and he can improve. PULL THE TRIGGER (8) is harder to trust off two heavy defeats, but his two wins from five starts at this track and distance keep him in the winning conversation. Draws much better this time around and the form out of his last start has been solid. Can play a leading role. BLOOD SAINT (5) was only beaten a neck first-up at this venue and drops sharply in weight, with a small but genuine track-and-trip record. FORBIDDEN APPLE (7) has been closing off honestly and her two wins from six at this track and distance give her a realistic way into the race if she sustains that finish. SHOOT TO FAME (9) has trialled well since a disappointing effort last start and can bounce back.",
